#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069968 :tutorial/content "A **root** of a polynomial is a value that will make the polynomial equal zero when substituted for the polynomial's variable.\n\nFor example, consider the polynomial $x^2-9$. This polynomial has two roots, $x=3$ and $x=-3$, because the polynomial evaluates to $0$ when either of these values is substituted for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx = 3⇒x^{2} - 9 &=  \\\\\n(3)^{2} - 9 &=  \\\\\n9 - 9 &=  \\\\\n0\\begin{vmatrix}✓ \\\\ x =-3⇒x^{2} - 9 &= \\\\ (-3)^{2} - 9|= \\\\ 9 - 9|= \\\\ 0\\end{vmatrix}✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nOn the other hand, a number like $x=1$ is *not* a root of the polynomial because the polynomial does not evaluate to $0$ when this value is substituted for $x$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nx = 1⇒x^{2} - 9 &=  \\\\\n(1)^{2} - 9 &=  \\\\\n1 - 9 &=  \\\\\n&= - 8 \\mid \\cdot\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "5b765b45-ae0c-5c2f-958b-e69d41100abc" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3321 :tutorial/title "Introduction"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069969 :tutorial/content "A **parametric polynomial** is a polynomial in which one of the coefficients is itself represented as another variable.\n\nFor example, the polynomial below is a parametric polynomial:\n\n$$\nf(x)=2x^2 -px\n$$\n\nHere, $p$ is a **parameter**, which means that it corresponds to a certain constant value. Unlike the variable $x$, the parameter is treated exactly like any other coefficient. It's only special in that we don't know its numerical value.\n\nIf we're given the root of a polynomial, we can find the numerical value of a parameter. Let's say, for instance, that a root of the above polynomial is $x=1$. This means that the polynomial is zero for that value:\n\n$$\nf(1)=0\n$$\n\nTherefore, we can evaluate the polynomial at $x=1$, set it equal to $0$, and solve the equation for the parameter $p$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\nf(1) &= 0 \\\\\n2(1)^{2} - p(1) &= 0 \\\\\n2 - p &= 0 \\\\\np &= 2\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "91fb2858-964a-50e9-a2fc-ae2af84b6b20" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3322 :tutorial/title "Solving for an Unknown Parameter Given the Root of a Polynomial"}]}
